        "original_id": "2b869340-ce8b-5f1f-b83a-0aa8b0847f58",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Buildings: One Liberty Plaza, 1717 Broadway, Barclay Tower, Singer Building, City Investing Building\n- Companies: U.S. Steel, Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP\n- Places: Lower Manhattan, Manhattan, Tribeca, New York City, North America\n- Topics: skyscrapers, hotel height, headquarters\n\nFacts:\n- One Liberty Plaza was formerly known as the U.S. Steel Building.\n- One Liberty Plaza is a skyscraper in Lower Manhattan in New York City.\n- One Liberty Plaza stands at the site of the former Singer Building and the former City Investing Building.\n- The Singer Building was the tallest structure ever dismantled.\n- 1717 Broadway is a skyscraper in Manhattan in New York City, United States.\n- 1717 Broadway is 750 feet tall.\n- 1717 Broadway is the tallest hotel in North America.\n- Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP is an international law firm headquartered at One Liberty Plaza in New York City.\n- Barclay Tower is a skyscraper in the Tribeca neighborhood of Lower Manhattan in New York City.",
